id:                     E14860
trigger_tool:           ctest|conan|runtime
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        Read-only file system.*tmp|temporary output defaults to /tmp despite TMPDIR
severity:               2
category:               portability,ohos,hmdfs,test
match_keywords:         TMPDIR,read-only /tmp,TEMP,TMP,library temporary path,writer test
title:                  Repair library-internal temporary path selection when it ignores POSIX TMPDIR
root_cause:             The build environment exports a writable TMPDIR, but library source checks only TEMP and TMP before hard-falling back to /tmp; the source never consumes the environment value expected by the test harness.
affected_scope:         POSIX library code or test helpers with their own temporary-directory selection chain and a read-only system /tmp.
verification_cmd:       Run the full upstream test inventory under a writable task-private TMPDIR and verify output creation plus an installed-package consumer; inspect source precedence for TEMP, TMP, and TMPDIR.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           add-tmpdir-before-system-fallback
rec_description:        Preserve existing explicit overrides, then consult TMPDIR before the hard-coded system fallback; configure a writable per-task directory and run the real writer tests.
rec_command:            patch temporary-directory selection; export TMPDIR=<task-private-writable-dir>; ctest --output-on-failure
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-selection-patch
forbid_1_pattern:       only-export-TMPDIR
forbid_1_reason:        Setting TMPDIR has no effect when the library code never reads it.
forbid_1_consequence:   Target writes still hit read-only /tmp and the upstream writer tests fail.
principles:             []
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E002, E547]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E14860-draft-2501.md
last_updated:           2026-10-04
source_event:           ptex/2.4.2 PtexWriter.cpp TMPDIR fallback patch; OHOS W3 ptex-w3-20261004T035557Z CTest 4/4 and installed consumer 1/1; raw log SHA-256 c0a8658b50636c51ad05c015387722bf592065560e30cfe197204488214ffa60.
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     1.0
metrics_last_used:      2026-10-04
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         2501
